      "description": "The NestJS idioms you know, their vibe.js form, and the error that points you there when the old form slips in."
    },
    {
      "path": "guides/coming-from-vue-router",
      "title": "Coming from vue-router and Vue Test Utils",
      "description": "The vue-router and Vue Test Utils idioms you know, their vibe.js form, and the error that points you there when the old form slips in."
    },
    {
      "path": "guides/coming-from-vue",
      "title": "Coming from Vue",
      "description": "What carries over from Vue 3 to vibe.js, the Vue idioms that change and the error code that reports each one, the APIs that behave differently, and what vibe.js leaves out."
    },
    {
      "path": "guides/editors",
      "title": "Editor setup",
      "description": "Type checking, hover, go to definition and diagnostics in .vibe files in VS Code, Neovim and other LSP editors, the known limitations, and how to fix a setup that shows no types."
    },
    {
      "path": "guides/extending",
      "title": "Extending vibe.js",
      "description": "Package reusable features as UI plugins and composables, and as configurable server modules, middleware, guards, interceptors, filters and metadata."
    },
    {
      "path": "guides/getting-started",
      "title": "Getting started",
      "description": "Create a vibe.js app, run it, check it, and set up your editor and coding agent."
    },
    {
      "path": "guides/tutorial",
      "title": "Tutorial",
      "description": "Build a users API and a page that lists the users, find a template type error with vibejs check, then build, serve and develop the app."
    },
    {
      "path": "index",
      "title": "vibe.js",
      "description": "A full-stack TypeScript framework where the UI, the server and the contract between them are type-checked end to end."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/configuration",
      "title": "Configuration",
      "description": "Typed environment config, logging, CORS, cookies, request limits, shutdown and the TypeScript setup of a vibe.js server."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/contracts",
      "title": "Contracts",
      "description": "Declare an API once with defineContract, serve it from a controller, call it from the UI with createClient and generate OpenAPI from it."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/handlers",
      "title": "Controllers and handlers",
      "description": "Serve a contract with @Controller and @Handle, read the typed ctx, raise declared errors and fix TS1241 on @Handle."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/index",
      "title": "Server",
      "description": "The layout of a vibe.js server application, how it is created, served and shut down, and what is deployed."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/modules",
      "title": "Modules and providers",
      "description": "Modules, providers, field injection with inject(), tokens, exports, global modules and lifecycle hooks."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/pipeline",
      "title": "Middleware, guards, interceptors and filters",
      "description": "The request pipeline of a vibe.js server, the run order of its enhancers, typed metadata and global enhancers."
    },
    {
      "path": "server/testing",
      "title": "Testing the server",
      "description": "Test modules in process with Test.createTestingModule, replace providers, call routes through the typed client and check the graph with inspect()."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/components",
      "title": "Components",
      "description": "Import components, declare props, events, slots and models with the define macros, pass attributes through, and expose values to template refs."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/data",
      "title": "Data loading",
      "description": "Load data with useAsync, keep it in sync with the route, abort stale requests, narrow typed API results and share state between components."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/index",
      "title": "UI essentials",
      "description": "Write a .vibe component, mount the app, handle errors and warnings, and find the pages on reactivity, templates, components, lifecycle and provide/inject."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/lifecycle",
      "title": "Lifecycle",
      "description": "The lifecycle hooks of a component, the order in which they run, and how errors travel through onErrorCaptured to app.config.errorHandler."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/provide-inject",
      "title": "Provide and inject",
      "description": "Pass values to every descendant of a component or to the whole app with provide and inject, typed by an InjectionKey."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/reactivity",
      "title": "Reactivity",
      "description": "Reactive state with ref, shallowRef, reactive, readonly and computed; side effects with watch and watchEffect; effect scopes, nextTick and shared state in composables."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/routing",
      "title": "Routing",
      "description": "Declare typed routes, render them with RouterView and RouterLink, read the route, guard navigations, load pages lazily and control scrolling."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/template-syntax",
      "title": "Template syntax",
      "description": "Interpolation, attribute bindings and spreads, class and style values, events and modifiers, conditions, keyed lists, v-show, v-model, template refs and dynamic components."
    },
    {
      "path": "ui/testing",
      "title": "Testing components",
      "description": "Test .vibe components and composables in Vitest with mount, wrappers, CSS selectors, events, props and the router."
    }
